# openapi-generator reads this file from its output directory — this one — and overwrites every
# file it emits under it, never deleting anything it does not. Nothing outside montecarlo/ is
# reachable, so the module files and the repository documentation need no entry here: the
# generator cannot write to the repository root at all.
#
# Verified by running the generator into an empty directory with no ignore file: it writes
# README.md, .gitignore, git_push.sh, .travis.yml and api/openapi.yaml, plus go.mod and go.sum
# unless withGoMod=false, which generate-go-sdk.sh passes. Those five entries are load-bearing;
# the rest are defensive, and are kept so the protected set reads as one list.
#
# This file is what api-codegen's generate-go-sdk.sh compares its PROTECTED array against,
# whole line for whole line; the root AGENTS.md documents this list entry for entry. A variant
# spelling still protects the file but fails that check.

# Client construction and credentials: NewClient, Options, the OAuth token source and the
# CLI's profiles file, plus example_test.go, the external-package example that compiles the
# public surface as a consumer would. Defensive: the generator names its files api_*.go,
# model_*.go, client.go, configuration.go, response.go and utils.go, and is run with test
# generation off.
auth.go
auth_test.go
oauth.go
oauth_test.go
profile.go
profile_test.go
example_test.go

# The package doc comment, which is the pkg.go.dev page for this package.
# Defensive: the Go generator emits no doc.go.
doc.go

# A go.mod here would make this package its own module, separate from the repository's.
# Defensive: generate-go-sdk.sh passes withGoMod=false, so neither file is emitted.
go.mod
go.sum

# Suppressed rather than protected. openapi-generator vendors a YAML copy of its input spec
# here by default; nothing in this repo or its consumers reads it, docs/ already documents
# every operation and model, and info.version is the API's major version so the copy cannot
# identify which export produced this SDK. Keeping it would publish the internal x-mc-*
# codegen markers the input carries. Load-bearing: remove this line and the generator writes
# the file again.
api/openapi.yaml

# The generator's README duplicates the root one and its example builds a client with no
# server URL; its .gitignore is Go scaffolding the root one covers. Both load-bearing —
# the generator emits both.
README.md
.gitignore

# The generator's own scaffolding, which we do not use. Both load-bearing: listing them is
# what keeps the generator from ever writing them, which is why neither exists in the tree.
git_push.sh
.travis.yml
